cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "stella-mcp: Model Context Protocol server for Stella system dynamics models"
authors:
  - family-names: Bradley
    given-names: Alex
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4044-2802"
    affiliation: "Department of Earth, Environmental, and Planetary Sciences, Washington University in St. Louis"
    email: abradley@wustl.edu
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets AI assistants
  programmatically create, read, validate, and modify Stella system
  dynamics models in the XMILE (.stmx) format. Supports building
  stock-and-flow diagrams from scratch, parsing existing models,
  checking for structural errors (undefined variables, missing
  connections), and exporting valid XMILE files that open in Stella
  Professional. Designed for teaching system dynamics, rapid
  prototyping via natural language, and batch model creation.
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - system dynamics
  - Stella
  - XMILE
  - stock and flow
  - simulation
  - biogeochemistry
  - teaching
